From 7a2ef774f3a24bf44650aee5586b096cb0c7d4b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:54:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! transaction(v2): integrate native transaction
 identities and serialization

Reject implicit legacy-script/address payout construction for native coinbases. Native miners provide an explicitly typed output policy; native address RPCs construct type0/type1 policies directly and preserve explicit legacy coinbase paths where consensus permits. Never reinterpret already committed roots or infer program language from byte patterns.

SetCoinbaseOutputs rejects mixed/legacy native payout configurations atomically, including miner-fund, staking, treasury and pool payees. Those policies need explicit native configuration before they can produce a native template. GBT placeholders use an explicit native OP_TRUE output. Focused regression asserts that a remote legacy address is rejected before accepting any block and that a genuine keyhash payout matures and spends with the existing BIP340 VM.

Causal owner: 15c667d89d introduces the BranchLeaf(legacy script) fallback. Later helper owner cead0ff611 needs the strict typed-output adapter; codec RPC support depends on address template b65d9d9b. This endpoint fixup must be distributed into those owners with prefix checks, not blindly autosquashed before its API prerequisites. Validation pending normal build; old binary accepts the forbidden payout, recorded in native-wallet-lifecycle/payout-before-2.log.
